esult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"call\": 3, \"returncode\": 0, \"stdout\": \"#0 declared: slot_system entity_role system  [proposed]\\r\\n#1 declared: slot_system is_a Slot System  [proposed]\\r\\n#2 declared: slot_system world_rule The Slot System grants specific magical permissions through installed skills. Every person receives exactly one Slot. Ordinary capacity is one installed skill; replacing it releases the old magic, not memory or mundane expertise. Reacquiring a released skill requires another source. No class grants extra skills.  [proposed]\\r\\n#3 declared: slot_system manifests_as Still white lettering on a faint charcoal field appears in personal vision without a voice. At Earth's arrival active phones, tills and televisions echo: EVERY PERSON HAS RECEIVED ONE SLOT. CHOOSE WHAT YOU WILL BE ABLE TO DO.  [proposed]\\r\\n#4 declared: slot_rank type criterion  [proposed]\\r\\n#5 declared: slot_rank is_a Slot Rank  [proposed]\\r\\n#6 declared: slot_rank comparator ordinal  [proposed]\\r\\n#7 declared: slot_rank governed_by (slot_system)  [proposed]\\r\\n#8 declared: slot_rank world_rule Installation earns no advancement. First successful control under real environmental demand, materially harder applications and genuinely new combinations earn progress. Easy repetition stops contributing; sustained practice can prepare harder feats. There are no fixed advancement quotas. Higher Slot Rank increases installed skills' strength and endurance, not their magical functions. Eight rungs describe the locally attested span, not a final ceiling.  [proposed]\\r\\n#9 declared: rank_1 precedes slot_rank (rank_2)  [proposed]\\r\\n#10 declared: rank_2 precedes slot_rank (rank_3)  [proposed]\\r\\n#11 declared: rank_3 precedes slot_rank (rank_4)  [proposed]\\r\\n#12 declared: rank_4 precedes slot_rank (rank_5)  [proposed]\\r\\n#13 declared: rank_5 precedes slot_rank (rank_6)  [proposed]\\r\\n#14 declared: rank_6 precedes slot_rank (rank_7)  [proposed]\\r\\n#15 d